  "summon_profile": null,
  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "sustained multi-strike preventing target HP recovery",
    "skill1": "dash to weakest enemy, dealing damage and knocking them up",
    "skill2": "battle-start enhanced state extended by assists or defeats; on exit, uncontrolled devour a non-summoned unit",
    "skill3": "life drain increases with assists and defeats",
    "skill4": "gain ATK and max HP on assist or defeat",
    "skill5": "after enough assists or defeats, ultimate recovers energy on cast"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Harak]] enters an **enhanced battle-start state** that extends with assists and defeats, then devours a non-summoned unit when the state ends. He dashes to the **weakest enemy**, knocks them up, and his ultimate blocks **target HP recovery** with sustained multi-strikes. Life Drain and **ATK plus max HP** grow with each takedown across the fight. Enough assists or defeats also **refund ultimate Energy** for another execute window. He snowballs hardest in **chaotic multi-kill fights** where bodies feed his ramp and devour timing. **Single-target stalls** or teams that deny assists keep him from growing or force bad devour targets on allies.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Harak]] opens in **feast mode**, dashing to weak targets and snowballing ATK/HP off assists and kills; when feast ends he **uncontrollably devours** the weakest non-summoned unit — ally or enemy — if they sit under his devour threshold. Deny the multi-kill chaos that extends feast and refunds his ultimate, and keep your weakest **above devour range**. He relocates too often for assassin pins — prefer lasting wide ultimates like [[Shemira]] or [[Frieren]], and cut his life-drain sustain with [[filter:heal-inhibitor]] like [[Gwyneth]] or [[Satrana]]. He is **Unaffected** during Vicious Bite and the devour — do not bank on interrupting those casts. His feast opener now casts a free Tidal Assault, so expect early damage and keep the weakest unit protected from it."
}
